<title>GERMANY: Euro not hurt by German deficit of 3.2 pct - FDP.</title>
<headline>Euro not hurt by German deficit of 3.2 pct - FDP.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The stability of Europe's planned single currency would not be hurt if Germany had a deficit ratio of 3.1 or 3.2 percent of economic output, head of Germany's junior coalition partners the Free Democrats said in an interview.</p>
<p>&quot;For the credibility of German policy, 3.0 (percent) would be better,&quot; Wolfgang Gerhardt told Stern magazine. &quot;But the stability of the euro would not be seriously endangered were it also 3.1 or 3.2 (percent).&quot;</p>
</text>
